From: TB710FU clean board
Subject: [PATCH] Record KMEM startup callback completion in the live log

Source: pinned XNU ac9718fb1af618d5ce8678d0dc6e8a58f252216f after the
selected arm64e, device pre-OS, macOS 27.3 and device 0001..0015 patches.
Reason: the live export ends at the verbose startup-entry line for KMEM rank 0.
That line is emitted before the callback and cannot show whether the callback
returned. When the live-log display initialized successfully, write one
completion marker after the callback and call the bounded live-log poll. The
existing global 250 ms frame throttle remains in force. This does not change VM
sizing, callback order or error handling.

Verification: applies after 0015 to the selected startup.c; the callback and
startup-entry cursor remain in their original order. Native arm64e compilation
and prelink must be rerun before this patch is used on a device.

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -494,5 +494,13 @@ kernel_startup_initialize_upto(startup_subsystem_id_t upto)
 		startup_phase = cur->subsystem - 1;
 		kernel_startup_log(cur->subsystem);
 		cur->func(cur->arg);
+#if defined(XNU_TB710FU_LIVE_LOG) && XNU_TB710FU_LIVE_LOG
+		if (tb710fu_live_log_active() &&
+		    cur->subsystem == STARTUP_SUB_KMEM &&
+		    cur->rank == STARTUP_RANK_FIRST) {
+			kprintf("TB710FU live log: KMEM rank-0 callback returned\n");
+			tb710fu_live_log_poll();
+		}
+#endif
 		startup_entry_cur = ++cur;
 	}
